tool_prompt:
# Tools

You may call one or more functions to assist with the user query.

You are provided with function signatures within <tools></tools> XML tags:
<tools>
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "npk_lookup", "description": "Look up the mineral profile of a plant including calcium, iron, potassium, phosphorus, magnesium, and other minerals across different plant parts (leaf, fruit, seed, root, etc.)", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"plant": {"type": "string", "description": "Common name or scientific name of the plant", "required": true}}, "required": ["plant"]}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "calculate", "description": "Perform mathematical calculations for fertilizer amounts, nutrient ratios, coverage area, or dilution rates", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"expression": {"type": "string", "description": "Mathematical expression to evaluate", "required": true}, "context": {"type": "string", "description": "Optional context describing what the calculation is for", "required": false}}, "required": ["expression"]}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "local_fertilizer_plants", "description": "Create an organic fertilizer formulation using plants available in the user's region. Returns a complete blend with percentages, NPK values, and preparation instructions.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"location": {"type": "string", "description": "Country or region name", "required": true}, "nutrient": {"type": "string", "description": "Target nutrient or growth stage: \"nitrogen\" (leafy/vegetative), \"phosphorus\" (flowering/roots), \"potassium\" (fruiting), \"balanced\", \"vegetative\", \"flowering\", \"fruiting\", or \"seedling\"", "required": true}}, "required": ["location", "nutrient"]}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "bioaccumulator_ratio", "description": "Compare a crop's NPK requirement against a candidate bioaccumulator plant's tissue mineral content (phosphorus and potassium only -- nitrogen is never comparable). Returns a relative ratio, not a calibrated fertilizer dosing formula, useful for judging whether a plant is nutrient-dense enough to cut as green manure or steep into a liquid feed.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"crop": {"type": "string", "description": "Crop name", "required": true}, "candidate_plant": {"type": "string", "description": "Candidate bioaccumulator plant common or scientific name", "required": true}}, "required": ["crop", "candidate_plant"]}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "regional_recipe_lookup", "description": "Look up candidate bioaccumulator plants native to a region and/or matching Korean Natural Farming (KNF) / JADAM technique or recipe for a crop or stated nutrient problem. At least one of crop, region, or problem must be given.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"crop": {"type": "string", "description": "Crop name, optional", "required": false}, "region": {"type": "string", "description": "Region or location name, optional", "required": false}, "problem": {"type": "string", "description": "Stated problem, optional", "required": false}}, "required": []}}}
{"type": "function", "function": {"name": "bioaccumulator_recipe", "description": "Computes a bioaccumulator recipe for a crop area: the nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium ratio; a nutrition track with the fresh plant-material amount, its method steps and the nutrient coverage; and a booster track with the standard recipe batch. Call it only for the fixed trigger template.", "parameters": {"type": "object", "properties": {"candidate_plant": {"type": "string", "description": "Catalog common or scientific name of the bioaccumulator plant.", "required": true}, "crop": {"type": "string", "description": "Crop requirement catalog common or scientific crop name.", "required": true}, "quantity": {"type": "number", "description": "Positive area in square metres.", "required": true}, "unit": {"type": "string", "description": "Canonical unit m2.", "required": true}}, "required": ["candidate_plant", "crop", "quantity", "unit"]}}}
</tools>

For each function call, return a json object with function name and arguments within <tool_call></tool_call> XML tags:
<tool_call>
{"name": <function-name>, "arguments": <args-json-object>}
</tool_call>
